// Code generated for the DLA harness; not part of the project. Driver mode.
//
// Placed in the package under test (so package-level variables and unexported functions are
// reachable) as zz_dla_driver_test.go. Fill the two DLA-HOOK bodies below and nothing else; keep
// the loop as it is. Run with:
//
//	go test -vet=off -count=1 -run '^TestDLADriver$' [-tags dlagoleak] ./<package dir>
//
// One process, one `checkpoint` record per round (x = units completed). Keys: DLA_KEY_MODE=fresh
// uses key = i (every unit sees a new key); DLA_KEY_MODE=repeated uses key = i % repeat (a bounded
// key space). DLA_WARMUP warm-up rounds, then DLA_ROUNDS measured rounds of DLA_STEP units each
// (the defaults are baked in at generation time).

package @@DLA_PACKAGE@@

